<Legal title="Privacy policy" updated="20 November 2026" description="How Doddo, provided by Aelius Venture Limited, collects and uses personal data.">
  <p>Aelius Venture Limited ("we") operates Doddo. This policy explains what personal data we collect, why, and your rights under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>

  <h2>1. Who this covers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Business owners</strong> who create an account.</li>
    <li><strong>Clients</strong> whose details a business enters, or who book through a business's booking page.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account details: email address, name, and the role you choose.</li>
    <li>Business details: name, opening hours, services, team members and policies.</li>
    <li>Booking details: client name, email, phone, appointment times and notes.</li>
    <li>Payment information is handled by Stripe. We do not store full card numbers.</li>
    <li>Technical data needed to run the service, such as session cookies that keep you signed in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the booking service, send confirmations and reminders, and take deposits.</li>
    <li>To keep accounts secure and prevent misuse.</li>
    <li>To meet legal and accounting obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our lawful bases are contract (providing the service), legitimate interests (securing and improving it), and legal obligation.</p>

  <h2>4. Who controls the data</h2>
  <p>For client records entered by a business, the business is usually the data controller and we act as its processor. For business accounts and our own marketing, we are the controller.</p>

  <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
  <p>We share data only with service providers we need to run Doddo: Google Firebase and Google Cloud (hosting, database, sign-in), Stripe (payments), and email and SMS providers that send messages on a business's behalf.</p>

  <h2>6. Retention</h2>
  <p>We keep account and booking data while the account is active and for a reasonable period afterwards to meet legal obligations. Businesses can delete client records and appointments at any time.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, object to or restrict processing, and ask for a copy of your data. Contact us to exercise these rights. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).</p>

  <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
  <p>Doddo uses essential cookies only, for sign-in. We do not use advertising cookies.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>Aelius Venture Limited. Email: <a class="text-brand-700 underline" href="mailto:privacy@doddo.co.uk">privacy@doddo.co.uk</a></p>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Registered company details and address: [to be added before launch].</p>
</Legal>
